//RS /// Linux gives the action a mount namespace, so declared virtual toolchain
//RS /// paths stay virtual in argv and the environment. macOS and Windows enforce
//RS /// the same read-only policy with ACL/sandbox rules but do not project a
//RS /// second filesystem namespace; translate only the declared mount paths at
//RS /// that adapter boundary. The action key still contains the canonical virtual
//RS /// spelling and therefore remains machine-independent.
